  "claim": "For every d there is eps_d > 0 such that every depth-d Frege refutation of the octahedral knot sphere's Kasteleyn-signed NAE formula NAE(K_k) (n = 4k^2 points) has size at least exp(n^{eps_d}): the binary left-pigeon principle reduces to SINK by succ = f, pred = g, SINK to one-sided grid Sperner (COUNT-TFNP-20261107-001A) and grid Sperner to the sphere (FLAT-STATES-20261107-001B) by decision trees of depth O(log N), and depth-d Frege refutations of the bijective pigeonhole principle need exp(N^{eps_d}) (Ajtai; Pitassi-Beame-Impagliazzo; Krajicek-Pudlak-Woods).",
